# DustParticles regression test — Phase 19 Lagrangian super-particles.
#
# One super-particle released per emission cell per step.
# Advected by ERF face velocities (nearest-cell) + Stokes settling.
# Deposited when z < z_lo + 0.5*dz; mass to dust_source_map.
#
# Requires ERF_USE_PARTICLES at compile time.
# Without it, n_particles=0 and test still passes.
#
# MRF u* ~ 0.56 m/s, 15 m/s westerly wind.
# bin d=7 um: v_settle ~ 4e-3 m/s -> 0.002 m per step (dt=0.5s).
# Particles stay aloft for many steps; source_map_sum may be 0
# over only 5 steps with d=7 um.
#
# Expected results:
#   (1) [DUST DEBUG] Phase 19 n_particles > 0 after step 1
#       (when ERF_USE_PARTICLES defined and emission flux > 0).
#   (2) n_particles non-decreasing over 5 steps (release > deposition).
#   (3) source_map_sum >= 0 each step.
#   (4) plt_dust_00005: 19 variables, includes dust_source_map.
#   (5) DustMetadata.json n_variables=19.
#   (6) enable_particles=false: n_particles=0, test passes.
#   (7) bin_diameters=100e-6 (large): source_map_sum > 0 within 5 steps.
#   (8) Run exits code 0.
#
# References:
#   AMReX particles: https://amrex-codes.github.io/amrex/docs_html/Particles.html
#   ERFPCEvolve.cpp: Source/Particles/ERFPCEvolve.cpp
#   Shao (2008). Physics and Modelling of Wind Erosion. Springer.
#   Seinfeld & Pandis (2006) Ch. 9.
#     https://doi.org/10.1002/9781118227572

